WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.870
Local inference can reduce dependence on external model services, but privacy still requires design.

2
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.186
Data boundaries include more than the prompt box.

3
00:00:10.186 --> 00:00:21.162
Files, attachments, chat histories, local logs, screenshots, exports, backups, shared folders, and connected tools can all carry information from the workflow.

4
00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:24.478
Before a workflow is repeated, classify the data.

5
00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:37.033
Public information, internal notes, project-confidential material, personal data, customer data, regulated data, and sensitive operational details may require different handling.

6
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.718
Some data may be fine for a local session.

7
00:00:39.718 --> 00:00:44.772
Other data may need redaction, approval, or a different workflow entirely.

8
00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:48.799
Do not assume every local workflow is safe for every dataset.

9
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:56.379
A model session may be local, but the output may be copied into email, documents, source control, tickets, or chat.

10
00:00:56.379 --> 00:01:01.275
Backups may sync files. Logs may preserve prompts or response fragments.

11
00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:06.171
A useful boundary follows the data after the model response is generated.

12
00:01:06.171 --> 00:01:13.119
Retention choices matter. Decide which prompts, outputs, settings, and exported files should be kept.

13
00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:16.752
Remove temporary material when it is no longer useful.

14
00:01:16.752 --> 00:01:22.042
Keep important records only where they belong and where access is appropriate.

15
00:01:22.042 --> 00:01:24.885
Privacy is both technical and behavioral.

16
00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:34.676
Device security, file permissions, workspace separation, redaction habits, cautious sharing, and clear review rules all support sovereign AI.

17
00:01:34.676 --> 00:01:41.309
The safest local workflow is explicit about what data enters, what leaves, and what remains stored.

18
00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:47.073
When the boundary is unclear, pause and decide before adding more files or automation.
